# Towers, a team game for drones flown by plan (domains/recreation/towers, plans/towers.md).
# This section is the commander app (domains/teleoperation/command), in the Blue seat of a
# practice game: its driver (`towers_commander --expect`) starts a fresh game server for each
# test. rules/ is the referee on its own, with no window; arduplane/ is the game server with
# ArduPlane SITL drones. The vocabulary here is shared by all three.

Section: Towers
  Launch: start the commander app on a practice game. Run `cargo run --release -- --serve --red nobody` in `domains/teleoperation/command`. The app starts a game server with six ArduPilot drones, and takes the Blue seat. With `--red nobody`, nobody commands Red, and its drones circle over their base
  Towers is a game for two teams of drones, Blue and Red. Each team has three T1-S VTOL
  drones and a [[base]] at one end of the field. Five radio [[tower]]s stand on the field. At
  the start, each team holds its home tower. The centre tower and the two flank towers are
  neutral.

  You do not fly the drones with sticks. You command your team from the commander app: you
  give each drone an order, and the drone flies it by plan in [[AGENT mode]]. To take a tower,
  send drones to circle it. Each tower that your team holds gives you one point each second.
  The first team to 500 points wins. If no team has 500 points after 8 minutes, the team with
  more points wins.

  A team does not see the whole field. It sees round its drones, its base and the towers that
  it holds. The rest of the field is in [[fog]].

  The pages here assume that the app is open on a practice game. [[The rules of Towers]] tells
  you how a tower changes sides, how to win and what the fog hides. [[The game with ArduPlane
  drones]] plays a whole game between two computer teams. To make a computer commander better,
  see [[Captains for Towers]].

Vocabulary:
  State: the game of Towers is in play | won by Blue | won by Red | a draw
    Shows: in play: the clock runs, and the scores go up
    Shows: won by Blue: the game stops, and it says BLUE WINS
    Shows: won by Red: the game stops, and it says RED WINS
    Shows: a draw: the game stops, and it says DRAW
  State: the time left is 0..480 s
    Set: wait until the clock shows {value}
    Shows: the clock shows {value} left
  State: the score of Blue is 0..1000 points
    Set: play until Blue has {value}
    Shows: the score of Blue is {value}
  State: the score of Red is 0..1000 points
    Set: play until Red has {value}
    Shows: the score of Red is {value}
  State: the towers held by Blue are 0..5
    Set: take towers until Blue holds {value}
    Shows: Blue holds {value} towers

  # The west and the east flank towers, and the drones in their circles.
  State: the west tower is held by Blue | held by Red | neutral
    Shows: held by Blue: the west tower is blue
    Shows: held by Red: the west tower is red
    Shows: neutral: the west tower is grey
  State: the control of the west tower is -100..100 %
    Shows: the control bar of the west tower is at {value} %
  State: the circle of the west tower is contested | quiet
    Shows: contested: the circle of the west tower flashes, because drones of the two teams are in it
    Shows: quiet: the circle of the west tower does not flash
  State: the Blue drones in the west circle are 0..3
    Set: send Blue drones to the west tower until {value} of them circle it
  State: the Red drones in the west circle are 0..3
    Set: wait until {value} Red drones circle the west tower
  State: the Blue drones on the ground in the west circle are 0..3
    Set: land Blue drones in the circle of the west tower until {value} of them stand there
  State: the east tower is held by Blue | held by Red | neutral
    Shows: held by Blue: the east tower is blue
    Shows: held by Red: the east tower is red
    Shows: neutral: the east tower is grey
  State: the control of the east tower is -100..100 %
    Shows: the control bar of the east tower is at {value} %
  State: the Red drones in the east circle are 0..3
    Set: wait until {value} Red drones circle the east tower

  # What Blue knows: the map of the Blue team.
  State: the Red scout is at its base | near a Blue drone | far from anything Blue | near the Blue home tower
    Shows: at its base: the Red scout is on the ground at the Red base
    Shows: near a Blue drone: the Red scout flies 100 m from a Blue drone, over the middle of the field
    Shows: far from anything Blue: the Red scout flies 100 m north of the east tower, and no Blue drone is near
    Shows: near the Blue home tower: the Red scout flies 100 m north of the Blue home tower
  State: the Red scout on the Blue map is seen | last seen | unknown
    Shows: seen: the Blue map shows the Red scout where it is now
    Shows: last seen: the Blue map shows the Red scout dim, where Blue last saw it, with the time since then
    Shows: unknown: the Blue map does not show the Red scout
  State: the age of the Red scout on the Blue map is 0..600 s
    Shows: the Blue map shows the Red scout with the age {value} s
  State: the east tower on the Blue map is held by Blue | held by Red | neutral
    Shows: held by Red: the Blue map shows the east tower red
    Shows: neutral: the Blue map shows the east tower grey

  Event: the game runs for 10 seconds
    Say: wait 10 seconds
  Event: the game runs for 20 seconds
    Say: wait 20 seconds
  Event: the game runs for 1 minute
    Say: wait 1 minute
  Event: the Red scout flies into the fog for 10 seconds
    Say: watch the Red scout fly away to the north-east, far from the Blue drones, and wait 10 seconds
  Event: a Blue drone flies near the east tower
    Say: order a Blue drone to fly to a point 70 m south-west of the east tower, outside its circle

  # The computer commander of a team (recreation_towers::Commander): its orders to the Blue
  # drones. The first Blue drone stands at the west end of the Blue base, the third at the east end.
  State: the order of the first Blue drone is none | take the west tower | take the centre tower | take the east tower | take the Blue home tower | take the Red home tower | hold | go home | go to a point
    Shows: the first Blue drone gets the order to {value}. In the app, the list of drones shows the order beside B1
  State: the order of the second Blue drone is none | take the west tower | take the centre tower | take the east tower | take the Blue home tower | take the Red home tower | hold | go home | go to a point
    Shows: the second Blue drone gets the order to {value}
  State: the order of the third Blue drone is none | take the west tower | take the centre tower | take the east tower | take the Blue home tower | take the Red home tower | hold | go home | go to a point
    Shows: the third Blue drone gets the order to {value}
  # The commander app (domains/teleoperation/command), in the Blue seat of a game on the server.
  State: the seat of the app is none | Blue | refused
    Shows: Blue: the top bar of the app says BLUE COMMANDER
    Shows: refused: the top bar of the app says why the server refused the seat
  State: the towers on the app's map are 0..5
    Shows: 5: the map shows the five towers, each with its circle and its control bar
  State: the selected drone is none | the first Blue drone | the second Blue drone | the third Blue drone
    Set: click {value} in the list of drones
    Shows: the first Blue drone: B1 is lit in the list of drones, and a ring goes round B1 on the map
  State: the west tower on the Blue map is held by Blue | held by Red | neutral
    Shows: held by Blue: the west tower on the map turns blue
    Shows: neutral: the west tower on the map is grey
  Event: the commander joins the game
    Say: wait until the top bar says BLUE COMMANDER
  Event: the commander selects the first Blue drone
    Say: click B1 in the list of drones, or press 1
  Event: the commander sends the selected drone to the west tower
    Say: click the west tower on the map
  Event: the commander holds the selected drone
    Say: click HOLD
  Event: the commander sends the selected drone home
    Say: click HOME
  Event: the game runs for 2 minutes
    Say: wait until the clock has run for 2 minutes

  Event: the computer commander of Blue decides
    Say: wait for the next decision of the computer commander. It decides once each second
  Event: the computer commander of Blue plays for 15 seconds
    Say: wait 15 seconds while the computer commander gives its orders, once each second

  # A whole game on the game server, with an ArduPlane SITL for each drone (the server's report).
  State: the drones in AGENT mode are 0..6
    Shows: 6: the report of the server says `RESULT in_agent=6`. All six drones flew the game in AGENT mode
  State: the commands that the drones refused are 0..100000
    Shows: 0: the report of the server says `RESULT refused=0`. The drones accepted every plan and every mode change
  State: the drones that crashed are 0..100
    Shows: 0: the report of the server says `RESULT crashes=0`
  State: the towers that Blue took are 0..100
    Shows: at least 1: the report of the server says `RESULT taken_blue=` with 1 or more
  State: the towers that Red took are 0..100
    Shows: at least 1: the report of the server says `RESULT taken_red=` with 1 or more
  State: the sightings from the fog on the Blue seat are 0..100000
    Shows: 0: a seat that watches Blue never gets a Red drone that Blue does not see, or the place of a Red drone that Blue does not see now
  State: the Red drones that the Blue seat saw are 0..3
    Shows: at least 1: a seat that watches Blue gets Red drones when Blue sees them
  Event: two computer teams play a game of Towers
    Say: wait for the end of the game. The server flies the drones with a computer commander for each team

  Phrase: a game of Towers is in play
    Say: wait until all the drones stand at their bases, and the clock shows 480 s
    Given the game of Towers is in play
    And the time left is 480 s
    And the score of Blue is 0 points
    And the score of Red is 0 points
    And the towers held by Blue are 1
    And the west tower is neutral
    And the control of the west tower is 0 %
    And the Blue drones in the west circle are 0
    And the Red drones in the west circle are 0
    And the Blue drones on the ground in the west circle are 0
    And the east tower is neutral
    And the control of the east tower is 0 %
    And the Red drones in the east circle are 0
    And the east tower on the Blue map is neutral
    And the Red scout is at its base
